ATTRIBUTION
===========

UltraOS is derived in part from the Atlas playbook
(https://github.com/Atlas-OS/Atlas), Copyright (C) AtlasOS contributors,
licensed GPL-3.0. The playbook structure, playbook.conf conventions, the
conservative service sets, deprovisioning patterns, and the post-install
toggle-folder concept are derived from Atlas. This attribution is required by
the GPL and deserved by the quality of the upstream work; the UltraOS project
is otherwise not affiliated with AtlasOS.

UltraOS is executed by AME Wizard. Its open-source backend,
TrustedUninstaller (https://github.com/Ameliorated-LLC/trusted-uninstaller-cli,
MIT), and ame-assassin (https://github.com/Ameliorated-LLC/ame-assassin, MIT)
are used unmodified at runtime by the wizard to apply playbook actions.

Design was further informed by the following projects. Ideas and design
patterns only were taken; no code or YAML was copied from the
non-GPL-compatible sources, and small snippets from permissive licenses are
credited in-line in the source files where they appear:

- ReviOS / MeetRevision playbook (https://github.com/MeetRevision/playbook,
  CC BY-SA 4.0) - engine-native browser flow, option UX, honest warning copy.
- Win11Debloat by Raphael Finch (https://github.com/Raphire/Win11Debloat,
  MIT) - the Sticky Keys shortcut-disable value (Flags=506) and several
  QoL registry patterns studied while designing UltraOS's equivalents.
- Chamber-Playbook (https://github.com/ChamberTechFPS/Chamber-Playbook,
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) - verification-manifest thinking, phased status text.
- winutil by ChrisTitusTech (https://github.com/ChrisTitusTech/winutil, MIT) -
  per-tweak original-value/undo data model, per-tweak documentation links.
- O&O ShutUp10++ (https://www.oo-software.com/en/shutup10) - privacy-toggle
  UX with per-setting recommendation levels (inspiration only).
- Remove-MS-Edge by ShadowWhisperer (https://github.com/ShadowWhisperer/
  Remove-MS-Edge, CC0-1.0) - studied as the reference Edge-removal mechanism
  when designing UltraOS's independent implementation.

